id: cold-weather
name: Cold Weather
kind: battlefield
weather: true
profile: elemental-ice
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The cold. Saving Throws roll 1(WT) lower, and past Natural it halves your Surgency
  and drains 10(bT) Ki Points a Combat Round.
text: >
  Cold Weather: The chilling cold seeps into your bones, freezing you to the core.

  Connected Profile: Elemental (Ice)

  Natural Weather (Tier 1) Effect(s):
  * Reduce the Dice Score of your Saving Throws by 1(WT).

  Unnatural Weather (Tier 2) Effect(s):
  * Halve your Surgency.

  Cataclysmic Weather (Tier 3) Effect(s):
  * At the start of each Combat Round, reduce your Ki Points by 10(bT).

---

# Hot Weather's mirror, rule for rule: a roll at Natural, a halved value at Unnatural, and
# ten a base Tier drained every Combat Round at Cataclysmic. The Tiers stack here for the
# same reason and are tested the same way.
#
# --- Natural (1) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce the Dice Score of your Saving Throws by 1(WT)."
#
# Your Saving Throws - all four of them. Written to `save.all` rather than to the four by
# name, because a file listing them is a list that would quietly miss a fifth. That Slot is
# applied outside the one named for a single Throw, so it lands on the finished value.
#
# The Dice Score, which is what the roll comes to. A Saving Throw rolls the Base Die plus
# its value, so reducing the value is reducing the score - there is no separate number for
# the roll the way there is for a Steadfast Check.
#
# --- Unnatural (2) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Halve your Surgency."
#
# Surgency is what a Surge adds to the Life and Ki Points it gives back, so halving it is
# halving what rest is worth in this cold. A multiplication on the finished value, the way
# Hot Weather halves the Soak Value.
#
# --- Cataclysmic (3) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "At the start of each Combat Round, reduce your Ki Points by 10(bT)."
#
# Ki rather than Life, which is the only thing that separates this from Hot Weather's third
# Tier - and it is the meaner of the two in a long fight, because Ki is what every Maneuver
# is paid for.
#
# The Round rather than the turn, so it lands once on everybody standing in it.
#
# --- What is not built ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Connected Profile: Elemental (Ice)." The Elemental Profiles are the Magic Profiles, and
# there are none in this system yet. Carried in the header and read by nobody.

[passive]
save.all -= 1(WT);

if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 2) {
  surgency *= 0.5;
}

[automatic/start-of-round]
if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 3) {
  ki.value -= 10(bT);
}
